                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Human anatomy is a core medical course focusing on the morphology, structure, and spatial relationships of human organ systems. Combining lectures, specimen observation, and lab practice, it covers nine major systems (e.g., musculoskeletal, digestive, respiratory) to build a morphological foundation for clinical medicine.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
